In .NET MAUI Shell, you can't directly intercept the hardware/software back button from the page level in a clean way, but here's the recommended approach:

**1. Custom "Cancel" button in the toolbar (replaces back arrow):**

```xml
<!-- EditProductPage.xaml -->
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="YourApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <ContentPage.Resources>
        <BackButtonBehavior x:Key="CancelBackButton"
                            TextOverride="Cancel"
                            Command="{Binding BackCommand}" />
    </ContentPage.Resources>

    <!-- your form here -->
</ContentPage>
```

Or inline:

```xml
<Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
    <BackButtonBehavior TextOverride="Cancel"
                        Command="{Binding BackCommand}" />
</Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
```

**2. Intercept navigation with a confirmation dialog:**

```csharp
// EditProductPage.xaml.cs
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    public bool HasUnsavedChanges { get; set; }

    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        BindingContext = this;
        BackCommand = new Command(OnBackRequested);
    }

    public ICommand BackCommand { get; }

    private async void OnBackRequested()
    {
        if (HasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave) return; // cancel navigation
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoBackAsync();
    }
}
```

**3. Handle the hardware back button (Android):**

```csharp
// EditProductPage.xaml.cs — add this override
protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
{
    // Returning true prevents default navigation
    if (HasUnsavedChanges)
    {
        MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(async () =>
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (leave)
                await Shell.Current.GoBackAsync();
        });

        return true; // suppress default back
    }

    return false; // allow default back
}
```

**Key points:**
- `BackButtonBehavior` replaces the shell back arrow with your "Cancel" text/command
- `OnBackButtonPressed()` handles the Android hardware/gesture back button
- On iOS, the swipe-back gesture isn't interceptable — the `BackButtonBehavior` command replaces the nav bar button, which is typically sufficient
